public static IEnumerable<T> EveryOther<T>(this IEnumerable<T> source) → source.Where((item, index) => index % 2 == 0)

Methods that use await must be marked `async`, and return Task<T>:
    async Task<int> FetchUserCountAsync() { ... }
Then await the calls: int count = await FetchUserCountAsync();

Start all the tasks first, then wait for them together:
    var tasks = products.Select(p => GetPriceAsync(p)).ToArray();
    decimal[] results = await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
    var prices = results.ToList();

Pass the token: await Task.Delay(50, ct);
using var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(200)); then pass cts.Token.
